    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Superb two bedroom open plan mid terrace home with a large garden ideally located in a quiet cul-de-sac.\r\n\r\nThis charming property features a gated driveway leading to an attractive façade. The entrance hall has a tiled floor and opens to a light filled dual aspect living room, dining area and kitchen. The living room enjoys solid wooden floors, a solid fuel stove and understairs storage. The eye catching U shaped kitchen boasts a tiled floor, splashback tiling and a Belfast sink. Double doors open to a sunny back garden with a paved patio with a pergola and rear pedestrian laneway access. Upstairs consists of two bedrooms and the family bathroom. Both double bedrooms have solid wood floors, while the main bedroom also has sophisticated sliderobes and an ornate fireplace. The accommodation is completed by a generous sized bathroom with a tiled floor and undersink storage. The attic is accessed via the landing.\r\n\r\n11 Kickham Road is perfectly situated in a quiet cul-de-sac between the villages of Inchicore & Kilmainham. There are a range of shops, bars, cafes and restaurants on your doorstep. The Phoenix Park, Grand Canal, Memorial Gardens, Royal Hospital & IMMA are all located in the area. The Red Line LUAS and Dublin Bike Station are a short stroll away making the city centre easily accessible. The new children's hospital at St. James's is also within walking distance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Year of construction 1930\r\nCul-de-sac location\r\nGated driveway\r\nLarge garden + rear access\r\nPatio & pergola\r\nOpen plan & dual aspect\r\nSolid wooden floors\r\nSolid fuel stove\r\nSliderobes\r\nBelfast sink"
      },
